		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5050&amp;p=36705#p36705"><![CDATA[
This problem is unlikely to be related to the OpenGD77 firmware, however in these instances you should always confirm the radio works correct using the official firmware, so that you can return it if faulty<br><br>You can reinstall the official firmware, but make sure that you install the correct version for the hardware revision / version of the radio.<br><br>These radios have completely separate hardware, i.e PLL and PA and IF etc for VHF and UHF, so its completely possibly that UHF works but VHF doesn't<br><br>Re:Calibration<br>The CPS does not have calibration screens for any of the newer radios. It only does backup / save / restore.<br><br>The firmware has a calibration screen for all radios, which allow the frequency and power to be calibrated, but the problem you describe sounds like its more than something that could be fixed by fine tuning the frequency adjustment or power output.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri Apr 11, 2025 8:48 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
