		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5050&amp;p=36704#p36704"><![CDATA[
I recently acquired a TYT MD-9600 thru an ebay auction that was an part of an estate sale.  Unit was never used, still in all plastic, not even programmed.<br><br>I installed the Open9600 firmware and programmed both analog and DMR channels for use as it was to be installed in my personal vehicle.<br><br>On the VHF side, I am showing interference coming in on ANY VHF frequency.  This is for both programmed channels and VFO mode.<br>I have also had reports that my transmission on VHF analog (VHF links to a UHF repeater) sounds like it is off frequency slightly.  Receive on my end sounds flawless.  For clarification, I do not have and diagnostic equipment at my disposal to check this as of this posting.  And the reports come from others using the repeater and other links during that same time-frame including the repeater trustee.  Another operator used and confirmed flawless operation of the link I was using.<br><br>The UHF side is fine.  No interference showing and reports of my transmissions are excellent.<br><br>Any ideas?  I've tried to open the calibration menu in software but I do not get a table shown to check any values.<br><br>Thanks in advance.  73's<br><br>KJ4BOL<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6761">KJ4BOL</a> — Fri Apr 11, 2025 5:43 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
